=begin
      author: Fizzleworth, Ashraam
        name: sac4mana
        game: gemstone
        tags: sorcerer, sacrifice, mana
    requires: Lich > 5.14.2
     version: 0.9
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Keeps a Sorcerer's mana topped off during a hunt via "sacrifice mana".

  Watches your mana. When it drops below the configured threshold and
  Sacrifice (Mana) specifically isn't on cooldown, it does "sacrifice mana"
  to refill. Each sacrifice ability -- Sacrifice (Mana), (Channel), (Infest),
  (Shift), (Fate) -- has its own independent cooldown, so this only checks
  for the "Mana" one; it won't be blocked by, say, Sacrifice (Channel) being
  on cooldown from animate_refresher.lic running alongside it.

  "sacrifice mana" itself spends shadow essence -- Infomon only updates its
  essence tracking once it parses the game's confirmation message, so
  sacrifice_mana() waits for that line before returning. Otherwise the
  essence check right after would still read the pre-sacrifice value.
  (That wait uses issue_command without quiet:true, so the confirmation
  text still displays normally -- quiet:true would silently swallow it
  from your screen entirely, not just from Lich's own echo.)

  room_target ignores your own minor demon AND any Animate Dead buddy
  (matched via IGNORE_NPCS = /verlok|animated/i) so wander/fizzsac never
  Pain/Tether/sacrifice your own pet or your ;reanim animate. (Observed
  2026-09-08: fizzsac spent a whole harvest cycle "You gesture at an
  animated supple Ivasian inciter" -- casting at Fizzleworth's own buddy.)
  Update the regex if you resummon a different demon type.

  ESSENCE: "sacrifice mana" spends shadow essence. The old wander+fizzsac
  cycle that tried to refill it (steps: pause bigshot -> wander to a new
  enemy -> appraise -> fizzsac -> repeat) is OFF by default (WANDER_HARVEST)
  and stays as dead code you can flip back on. It never worked for a
  mana-starved sorcerer: fizzsac needs several Pain casts to bring a FRESH
  creature to the ~2/3-health "enticingly frail" state sacrifice requires,
  and on <50 mana it either can't afford that or overshoots into a corpse
  (dead creatures give no essence). Proven repeatedly 2026-09-09.

  Essence now rebuilds from creatures the HUNT already softened, not fresh
  ones:
    - Fizzleworth-attack-ultima sacrifices its own tethered dying target
      during the Maelstrom hold while essence is low
    - Fizzleworth-anim-cleanup sweeps the room for frail creatures at end
      of hunt, before the walk home
  This script just keeps "sacrifice mana" running as the mana top-off; if
  essence hits bottom it backs off ~5 min and lets bigshot's oom rest carry
  the hunt. A hard-drained pool still needs a manual rebuild.

  Meant to run alongside fizzsac.lic during a hunt.

  Usage:  ;sac4mana
  Stop:   ;kill sac4mana
=end

module Sac4Mana
  # === config (edit to taste) ===================================================
  MANA_THRESHOLD        = 50
  CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS = 10
  FIZZSAC_SPELL_ID       = "719"   # spell fizzsac is told to use when harvesting after a mana sac
  BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME    = "bigshot"
  # Whichever Fizzleworth attack script is active (an A/B/C set --
  # -wing with Energy Wings, -base without, -cat = Corrupt Essence / Dark
  # Catalyst / Pain) owns the rotation and holds for its DoTs --
  # with_bigshot_paused only pauses "bigshot" by name,
  # which does nothing to a script bigshot merely started and is waiting on.
  # Without this check, a mana dip mid-rotation would send "sacrifice mana"
  # into the same roundtime, and worse, the harvest cycle's wander.lic would
  # start walking the room while the attack script is still mid-fight with the
  # original target. So just skip this poll and retry in
  # CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS instead of racing it -- bigshot's own oom rest is
  # the backstop if mana stays low longer than that.
  FIZZLEWORTH_ATTACK_SCRIPT_NAMES = ["Fizzleworth-attack-wing", "Fizzleworth-attack-base", "Fizzleworth-attack-cat", "Fizzleworth-attack-ultima"]
  ESSENCE_MAX            = 5
  # The wander+fizzsac harvest cycle is OFF by default: it wanders to FRESH
  # full-health creatures, which fizzsac can't Pain down to "frail" on <50
  # mana without overshooting into a corpse (= 0 essence) -- proven repeatedly
  # 2026-09-09. Essence now rebuilds via the attack rotation sacrificing its
  # own tethered dying targets + Fizzleworth-anim-cleanup's end-of-hunt sweep.
  # Set true to re-enable the old wander cycle.
  WANDER_HARVEST        = false
  MAX_HARVEST_ROUNDS     = 5      # give up wander+fizzsac cycling after this many rounds
  MAX_WANDER_SKIPS       = 5      # give up skipping "too easy" targets after this many wander attempts
  IGNORE_NPCS            = /verlok|animated/i   # your own minor demon / Animate Dead buddy -- never a harvest target
  TOO_EASY_REGEX         = /too easy for the likes of you/i

  # === helpers ===================================================================
  def self.sacrifice_on_cooldown?
    Effects::Cooldowns.to_h.keys.any? { |k| k.to_s =~ /sacrifice\s*\(\s*mana\s*\)/i }
  end

  def self.with_bigshot_paused
    paused_it = Script.running?(BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME) && !Script.paused?(BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME) && Script.pause(BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME)
    echo "Paused #{BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME}." if paused_it
    yield
  ensure
    if paused_it
      Script.unpause(BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME)
      echo "Unpaused #{BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME}."
    end
  end

  # @return true if it actually refilled mana, false if it couldn't (no
  # essence -> "too depleted", or nothing came back).
  def self.sacrifice_mana
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    lines = Lich::Util.issue_command(
      "sacrifice mana",
      /mana surge into you!|overwhelm you with shadow essence|too depleted of shadow essence/,
      include_end: false, silent: true
    )
    sleep 0.2
    waitrt?
    if lines.any? { |l| l =~ /too depleted of shadow essence/i }
      echo "!! Shadow essence exhausted -- 'sacrifice mana' can't refill. You're in a spiral:"
      echo "!! no essence -> no mana recovery -> can't afford to Pain a creature down to harvest."
      echo "!! Fix: a manual essence run somewhere easy with mana to spare (;fizzsac <#id> 719)."
      return false
    end
    lines.any? { |l| l =~ /mana surge into you|overwhelm you with shadow essence/i }
  end

  def self.room_target
    return "##{GameObj.target.id}" if GameObj.target and GameObj.target.name !~ IGNORE_NPCS

    npc = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n.status !~ /dead|gone/i and n.name !~ IGNORE_NPCS }
    npc ? "##{npc.id}" : nil
  end

  def self.too_easy?(target)
    lines = Lich::Util.issue_command(
      "appraise #{target}",
      /^The .+? is \w+ in size/,
      include_end: false, silent: true
    )

    if lines.any? { |line| line =~ TOO_EASY_REGEX }
      echo "#{target} is too easy for the likes of you."
      true
    else
      echo "#{target} is sacrifice worthy."
      false
    end
  end

  def self.find_worthy_target
    MAX_WANDER_SKIPS.times do
      Script.run("wander")

      target = room_target
      return nil unless target

      if too_easy?(target)
        echo "Wandering for something else."
        next
      end

      return target
    end

    nil
  end

  # Pain (711) is ~11 mana and it takes several to weaken a fresh creature the
  # ~2/3 health that sacrifice needs. If we can't afford even a couple, the
  # harvest is hopeless flailing -- fizzsac will just spam "not enough mana".
  def self.can_afford_to_harvest?
    (checkmana.to_i rescue 0) >= (Spell[711].mana_cost.to_i.positive? ? Spell[711].mana_cost.to_i : 11) * 2
  end

  def self.harvest_until_full
    unless can_afford_to_harvest?
      echo "Too low on mana to Pain a creature down for sacrifice -- skipping the harvest cycle."
      echo "Rebuild shadow essence with a manual run somewhere you have mana to spare."
      return
    end

    MAX_HARVEST_ROUNDS.times do |round|
      if Resources.shadow_essence.to_i >= ESSENCE_MAX
        echo "Shadow essence full (#{ESSENCE_MAX}/#{ESSENCE_MAX})."
        return
      end

      before = Resources.shadow_essence.to_i
      echo "Harvest round #{round + 1}/#{MAX_HARVEST_ROUNDS}: wandering for a worthy target."
      target = find_worthy_target

      unless target
        echo "Wander found nothing targetable/worthy -- stopping harvest cycle."
        return
      end

      echo "Target #{target} found, running fizzsac to harvest essence."
      Script.run("fizzsac", "#{target} #{FIZZSAC_SPELL_ID}")

      # made no progress and now can't afford to keep trying -> stop
      if Resources.shadow_essence.to_i <= before && !can_afford_to_harvest?
        echo "No essence gained and out of mana to keep trying -- stopping harvest cycle."
        return
      end
    end

    echo "Gave up harvesting after #{MAX_HARVEST_ROUNDS} rounds (essence: #{Resources.shadow_essence.to_i}/#{ESSENCE_MAX})."
  end

  # === main ======================================================================
  def self.run
    echo "Sac4Mana started! Watching mana (threshold: #{MANA_THRESHOLD})."
    echo "Stop with ;kill sac4mana"

    spiral_backoff_until = Time.now

    loop do
      if mana < MANA_THRESHOLD and !sacrifice_on_cooldown? and Time.now >= spiral_backoff_until and
         FIZZLEWORTH_ATTACK_SCRIPT_NAMES.none? { |n| Script.running?(n) }
        echo "Mana below #{MANA_THRESHOLD}, sacrificing mana to top off."
        got_mana = false
        with_bigshot_paused do
          got_mana = sacrifice_mana
          harvest_until_full if WANDER_HARVEST && Resources.shadow_essence.to_i < ESSENCE_MAX
        end
        # essence-spiral (couldn't sacrifice for mana and still can't harvest):
        # stop pausing bigshot every 10s just to fail -- let its own oom rest
        # carry the hunt and re-check in a few minutes.
        if !got_mana && Resources.shadow_essence.to_i <= 1
          spiral_backoff_until = Time.now + 300
        end
      end

      sleep CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS
    end
  end
end

Sac4Mana.run
